  "code": "prices = [3.5, 3.1, 2.2, 4.0, 2.8]\nhighest = prices[0]\nfor p in prices:\n    if p > highest:\n        highest = p\nprint(highest)                     # 4.0\norders = [\"Latte\", \"Mocha\", \"Tea\", \"Chai\"]\nn = len(orders)\nfirst = orders[0]\nfor i in range(n - 1):\n    orders[i] = orders[i + 1]\norders[n - 1] = first\nprint(orders)",
